If $f(a)=b$ and $f(b)=4$, then what is the value of $a-b$?

solution:
We can rewrite each fraction as $\frac{1}{n(n+1)}$.
So the sum becomes $\frac{1}{1\times2} + \frac{1}{2\times3} + \frac{1}{3\times4} + \frac{1}{4\times5} + \frac{1}{5\times6} = \frac{1}{1\times2} + \frac{1}{2\times3} + \frac{1}{3\times4} + \frac{1}{4\times5} + \frac{1}{5\times6} = \frac{1}{1} - \frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{3} + \frac{1}{3} - \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{5} + \frac{1}{5} - \frac{1}{6} = 1 - \frac{1}{6} = \boxed{\frac{5}{6}}$.
The answer is \frac{5}{6}

