If $f(a)=b$ and $f(b)=4$, then what is the value of $a-b$?

solution:
First, we can rewrite $0.\overline{09}$ as a fraction:
\begin{align*}
0.\overline{09} &= \frac{9}{99} \\
&= \frac{1}{11}.
\end{align*}
Similarly, we can rewrite $0.\overline{7}$ as a fraction:
\begin{align*}
0.\overline{7} &= \frac{7}{9}.
\end{align*}
Multiplying these fractions gives us:
\begin{align*}
\left( \frac{1}{11} \right) \left( \frac{7}{9} \right) &= \frac{1 \cdot 7}{11 \cdot 9} \\
&= \frac{7}{99}.
\end{align*}
So, $(0.\overline{09})(0.\overline{7}) = \boxed{\frac{7}{99}}$.The answer is \frac{7}{99}

